# vendor/sources.manifest -- pinned upstream sources for dossage.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated, one entry per line, '#' for comments):
#
#     <name>  <url>  <ref>  <sha>
#
# <name>  directory name under vendor/ that fetch-sources.sh clones into
# <url>   git clone URL
# <ref>   branch or tag to track (used when sha == PIN_ME to resolve, and
#         for documentation purposes once a concrete SHA is pinned)
# <sha>   40-char commit SHA to check out, or PIN_ME to fetch the tip of <ref>
#
# Run `./scripts/fetch-sources.sh --resolve` to resolve any PIN_ME entries;
# copy the printed SHAs back into this file to pin.

# SDL3, same pin as the shared sdl3-dos patch series in
# .sdl-dos-ports/shared/patches/sdl3-dos/ was built against (verified
# against doskutsu's own vendor/sources.manifest, which the shared patch
# series was extracted from). Must be a post-PR-#15377 commit -- that PR
# added the DOS backend.
SDL            https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL.git             main             74a746281f2208e07a7680560fcb7ec57565228e

# NOTE: SDL3_mixer is deliberately NOT vendored (confirmed once the actual
# SDL 1.2 -> SDL3 migration was done, see patches/passage/0001). Passage's
# audio is a from-scratch software synth over a raw sample callback, opened
# directly against core SDL3's SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream -- that reaches
# the DOS backend's SB16/OPL/GUS devices on its own; SDL3_mixer only adds
# file-format decode / multi-channel mixing convenience on top, neither of
# which this port uses. Do not add it back without a concrete reason.

# NOTE: SDL_image is deliberately NOT vendored. Passage's .tga graphics are
# decoded by minorGems' own TGAImageConverter (a small, self-contained
# uncompressed-TGA reader) -- no PNG/libpng dependency exists in the
# original engine, so there is nothing for SDL_image to do here. Do not
# add it back without a concrete reason found during porting.

# Passage (Jason Rohrer, 2007). Author's own GitHub account -- verified by
# direct clone: 2-commit tree, "Exported latest revision from sourceforge
# cvs, discarding history." This is the canonical upstream, not a fork or
# mirror. Public domain (see LICENSE-REVIEW.md).
passage        https://github.com/jasonrohrer/Passage.git        master           2f713f261dc907f6feda106ebbee0464eeab791d

# minorGems -- Jason Rohrer's own utility library; Passage's build depends
# on a small subset of it (see PLAN.md's research notes). Public domain,
# verified via its own in-repo no_copyright.txt (see LICENSE-REVIEW.md).
# Pin is current HEAD as of this research pass (2026-08-26) -- a starting
# point, not a confirmed-compatible revision. minorGems is a large,
# actively-developed library used by much newer projects (OneLife, etc.);
# if the compile phase hits API drift in the small subset Passage uses,
# walk this pin backward toward Passage's own era (2010-2017) before
# patching around a moving target -- see PLAN.md's "Open pin risk" note.
minorgems      https://github.com/jasonrohrer/minorGems.git      master           ef42b1ce511f2d355d5fc898fcce0b0af3a76d62
